.TH TESTULE 1 "September 2026" "testule v1alpha1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
testule \- portable testing contracts, normalized evidence, and gap analysis
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B testule validate
[--format text|json] <plan.yaml|->
.br
.B testule fingerprint
<plan.yaml|->
.br
.B testule gaps
[--format text|json] [--evidence-format document|jsonl] --subject-revision <revision> <plan.yaml|-> [evidence.yaml|- ...]
.br
.B testule go test
--plan <plan> --subject-revision <rev> --workspace <dir> --package <./pkg> --target <TestName> --level <level> --environment <id> --run-id <id> [--format text|jsonl] [--generation example] [--behavior <behavior>] [--visibility <visibility>] [--quality <attribute>] [--timeout 30s]
.br
.B testule go fuzz
--plan <plan> --subject-revision <rev> --workspace <dir> --package <./pkg> --target <FuzzName> --level <level> --environment <id> --run-id <id> [--format text|jsonl] [--behavior <behavior>] [--visibility <visibility>] [--quality <attribute>] [--fuzztime 1s] [--timeout 30s]
.br
.B testule go replay
--evidence <evidence.json> --subject-revision <rev> --workspace <dir> --environment <id> --run-id <id> [--timeout 30s]
.br
.B testule go promote
--evidence <evidence.json> --subject-revision <rev> --workspace <dir>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Testule is a CLI-first capability layer for portable testing contracts, ecosystem-native adapters, normalized Evidence, and evidence-based gap analysis. Normal commands are non-interactive and intended to compose predictably in shells, CI systems, and governed agent or supervisor transports.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate
Strictly decode and validate one TestPlan. A plan path of \fB-\fR reads the plan from standard input.
.TP
.B fingerprint
Compute the canonical TestPlan fingerprint. A plan path of \fB-\fR reads the plan from standard input.
.TP
.B gaps
Evaluate Evidence against a TestPlan and subject revision. With \fB--evidence-format=document\fR, each evidence input contains one Evidence document. With \fB--evidence-format=jsonl\fR, each evidence input is a bounded JSONL stream containing one strict Evidence object per physical line. At most one positional input may be \fB-\fR in an invocation.
.TP
.B go test
Execute one exact Go test through the incubating native Go adapter. \fB--format=jsonl\fR emits the normalized Evidence record to stdout.
.TP
.B go fuzz
Execute one bounded native Go fuzz target. \fB--format=jsonl\fR emits the normalized Evidence record to stdout.
.TP
.B go replay
Replay a previously captured Go fuzz Evidence record. This adapter-specific surface currently requires file input.
.TP
.B go promote
Explicitly promote a replayable fuzz failure into a persistent regression corpus entry. This mutates the workspace and currently requires file input.
.SH STANDARD STREAMS
.SS stdin
Where a read-only plan or evidence path accepts streaming, \fB-\fR denotes stdin. The binding must be unambiguous. Multiple positional \fB-\fR inputs are rejected with exit status 2.
.SS stdout
Stdout contains only requested primary result data. Machine formats are suitable for downstream parsing; operator diagnostics and warnings do not belong on stdout.
.SS stderr
Stderr contains usage diagnostics, human-oriented validation diagnostics in text mode, adapter/runtime failures, and other operator-facing context that is not part of the selected machine result.
.SH FORMATS
.TP
.B text
Human-readable command output. Text output is not a stable interchange format.
.TP
.B json
Single-document structured output used by validation and gap analysis.
.TP
.B jsonl
Record-stream output/input. Each physical line is one complete strict JSON Evidence object. Blank lines, malformed records, truncated records, and unknown fields are rejected. A complete final record need not end in a newline. Current bounds are 1 MiB per Evidence record, 16 MiB per input stream, and 128 records per input stream.
.PP
Evidence JSONL uses the Evidence object's own \fBapiVersion\fR and \fBkind\fR for schema identity. Stream transport does not rewrite plan fingerprints, subject revisions, metadata, or provenance.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed and its success condition is satisfied.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected Testule defect or invariant failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid CLI invocation or ambiguous stream binding.
.TP
.B 3
Invalid Testule declarative document, malformed normalized Evidence stream, or incompatible declarative input.
.TP
.B 4
I/O, adapter setup, dependency, or bounded execution error.
.TP
.B 5
Gap evaluation completed correctly but required gaps remain.
.TP
.B 6
Native adapter execution completed with a failed test or fuzz result.
.TP
.B 7
Requested adapter capability is unsupported.
.SH SIGNALS AND BROKEN PIPES
EPIPE and closed-pipe write failures are normal downstream pipeline termination and are not reported as Testule internal failures. Native SIGPIPE termination is likewise not a Testule invariant failure. Mutation-capable commands must not leave undocumented partially committed state.
.SH INTERACTION
Normal commands do not prompt, open editors or browsers, request terminal credentials, or require a controlling TTY. Any future interactive workflow must be explicitly selected.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The current core CLI defines no Testule-specific environment variables. Adapter subprocesses inherit the bounded execution environment described by the adapter contract; callers should not rely on undeclared environment state as portable Testule input.
.SH FILES
TestPlan and Evidence files are explicit command inputs. The Go adapter persists normalized Evidence and artifacts under its documented adapter output paths and may mutate a fuzz corpus only through the explicit \fBgo promote\fR operation. Testule does not define a global per-user state directory in v1alpha1.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate from stdin and inspect machine output:
.PP
.nf
cat plan.yaml | testule validate --format json - | jq -e '.valid'
.fi
.PP
Inspect unsatisfied gaps:
.PP
.nf
testule gaps --subject-revision "$REV" --format json plan.yaml evidence/*.yaml \\
  | jq '.entries[] | select(.state != "satisfied")'
.fi
.PP
Fan in evidence paths with xargs:
.PP
.nf
find evidence -name '*.yaml' -print0 \\
  | xargs -0 testule gaps --subject-revision "$REV" --format json plan.yaml
.fi
.PP
Preserve an Evidence stream while consuming it:
.PP
.nf
set -o pipefail
testule go test --plan plan.yaml --subject-revision "$REV" \\
  --workspace . --package ./pkg --target TestThing --level unit \\
  --environment ci --run-id run-1 --format jsonl \\
  | tee evidence.jsonl \\
  | testule gaps --evidence-format jsonl --subject-revision "$REV" \\
      --format json plan.yaml -
.fi
.SH CONFORMANCE
The repository validates this man page against the CLI's executable usage inventory and runs process-level tests for stdin composition, structured stdout/stderr separation, exit-code classes, non-interactive behavior, Evidence JSONL pipelines, and EPIPE handling.
.SH SEE ALSO
The repository documentation includes \fBdocs/cli-unix-composability.md\fR and \fBdocs/evidence-streaming.md\fR. The current interface is incubating and versioned as v1alpha1.
